From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nate Isern <nate@oxy.so>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make Astro's Mojo interfaces reachable from its own pages

A WebUI controller that implements a Mojo interface and overrides
`BindInterface` for it is still unreachable until the interface appears in the
frame binder map: `RenderFrameHostImpl` looks the interface up there, finds
nothing, and drops the request. The page sees a pipe that never answers. There
is no error, on either side.

This registers Astro's three interfaces, and the split between them IS the
grant -- which is the whole reason there are three:

  astro.mojom.ThemeProvider              read-only. EVERY Astro page binds it,
                                         so a colour change re-themes settings,
                                         the new tab page and the native UI at
                                         once.

  astro.settings.mojom.PageHandlerFactory  writes the theme. Granted to the
                                         settings controller alone, which is
                                         also the only surface holding the
                                         settingsPrivate grant (patch 060).

  astro.ntp.mojom.PageHandlerFactory     the new tab page's own data plane --
                                         widgets, links, notes, tiles, search.
                                         Granted to that page and nothing else.

A single read-write interface would have made every page that wants to READ
the theme able to CHANGE it, which is a grant nobody would have written down
deliberately.

Note the shape of the ThemeProvider line: ONE registration listing both
controllers. `RegisterWebUIControllerInterfaceBinder` DCHECKs on a second
registration of the same interface, so adding a page as its own line aborts a
developer build at startup rather than widening the grant.

The `allow_circular_includes_from` entry is a separate matter from the binders
and is here because it is the same patch's dependency edge. Astro's new tab
page builds its most-visited tiles from `ntp_tiles::MostVisitedSites`, and the
only way to construct one is `ChromeMostVisitedSitesFactory`, which is a source
of `//chrome/browser` itself. `//chrome/browser` already depends on
`//chrome/browser/oxy:webui_controllers` (below), so a dependency back would be
a cycle; this is Chromium's own mechanism for exactly that, and the list it
joins is forty entries of the same shape.

Registered in the desktop parts file, not the all-platforms one, to match
where the configs themselves are registered: inside the non-Android branch of
chrome_web_ui_configs.cc. The `//chrome/browser` dependency on
`//chrome/browser/oxy:webui_controllers` is in the same non-Android branch and
covers both halves of what this file needs -- the controllers' own headers, and
the generated mojom headers, which arrive through that target's `public_deps`
on `//chrome/browser/oxy/webui:mojo_bindings` and must EXIST before this file
compiles, not merely link afterwards.

Owned by https://github.com/OxyHQ/Astro/issues/15 and
https://github.com/OxyHQ/Astro/issues/22.
---
diff --git a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
--- a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
@@ -1552,7 +1552,15 @@ static_library("browser") {
     # TODO(crbug.com/394204688): Remove this once we ensure that
     # `PreconnectFromKeyedService` does not cause any regressions.
     "//chrome/browser/navigation_predictor:navigation_predictor",
     "//chrome/browser/optimization_guide:impl",
+
+    # Astro's new tab page builds its most-visited tiles from
+    # ntp_tiles::MostVisitedSites, and the only way to construct one is
+    # ChromeMostVisitedSitesFactory, which is a source of THIS target rather
+    # than of a component. Same reason as the entries above and the same
+    # mechanism: the dependency edge already runs this way, so the include
+    # needs permission rather than a second edge back.
+    "//chrome/browser/oxy:webui_controllers",
     "//chrome/browser/passage_embeddings",
     "//chrome/browser/permissions",
     "//chrome/browser/policy/messaging_layer/storage_selector",
@@ -4255,6 +4262,7 @@ static_library("browser") {
       "//chrome/browser/media/router/discovery/access_code:access_code_sink_service",
       "//chrome/browser/metrics/desktop_session_duration",
       "//chrome/browser/new_tab_page/chrome_colors",
+      "//chrome/browser/oxy:webui_controllers",
       "//chrome/browser/page_content_annotations:fetcher",
       "//chrome/browser/password_manager/password_change",
       "//chrome/browser/performance_manager/public/user_tuning",
diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders_webui_parts_desktop.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders_webui_parts_desktop.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders_webui_parts_desktop.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders_webui_parts_desktop.cc
@@ -22,6 +22,11 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/new_tab_page/modules/v2/most_relevant_tab_resumption/most_relevant_tab_resumption.mojom.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/new_tab_page/modules/v2/tab_groups/tab_groups.mojom.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/new_tab_page/new_tab_page_util.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/oxy/webui/astro_ntp.mojom.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/oxy/webui/astro_ntp_ui.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/oxy/webui/astro_settings.mojom.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/oxy/webui/astro_settings_ui.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/oxy/webui/astro_theme.mojom.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/lens/lens_overlay_untrusted_ui.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/lens/lens_side_panel_untrusted_ui.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/omnibox/omnibox_next_features.h"
@@ -597,6 +600,34 @@ void PopulateChromeWebUIFrameBindersPartsDesktop(
         DefaultBrowserModalUI>(map);
   }
 #endif
+
+  // Astro's own typed transports. Without an entry in this map the interface
+  // is unreachable from the page: the controller's BindInterface is never
+  // called and the request is dropped, which the page sees as a pipe that
+  // never answers rather than as a missing registration.
+  //
+  // They are granted separately and to different scopes on purpose.
+  // ThemeProvider is READ-only and EVERY Astro page gets it -- which is what
+  // makes a colour change in settings re-theme the new tab page live, in every
+  // open tab, with no reload. The interface is registered ONCE with the whole
+  // list of controllers that may bind it: the helper DCHECKs on a second
+  // registration of the same interface, so a page added as its own line here
+  // would not merely be redundant, it would abort a developer build at
+  // startup.
+  RegisterWebUIControllerInterfaceBinder<astro::mojom::ThemeProvider,
+                                         astro::AstroSettingsUI,
+                                         astro::AstroNtpUI>(map);
+
+  // Writing the theme is the settings page's alone, and so is the
+  // settingsPrivate grant that comes with upstream's host (patch 060).
+  RegisterWebUIControllerInterfaceBinder<
+      astro::settings::mojom::PageHandlerFactory, astro::AstroSettingsUI>(map);
+
+  // The new tab page's own data plane -- its widgets, links, notes, tiles and
+  // search. Granted to that page and to nothing else, which is why it is a
+  // separate interface from the theme it also reads.
+  RegisterWebUIControllerInterfaceBinder<astro::ntp::mojom::PageHandlerFactory,
+                                         astro::AstroNtpUI>(map);
 }
 
 void PopulateChromeWebUIFrameInterfaceBrokersTrustedPartsDesktop(
